  "ingredients": [
    "12 ounce salmon",
    "2 ounce bacon (diced)",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "1/4 medium yellow onion (sliced)",
    "1/4 cup chicken stock",
    "1 tablespoon tomato paste",
    "1/2 cup heavy cream",
    "1/4 cup fresh basil (thinly sliced)",
    "1/2 teaspoon lemon zest (grated)",
    "200 gram zucchini (spiralized)",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Gather and prep all of your ingredients.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add bacon into a pan over medium heat and cook until crisp. Remove bacon from the pan and set aside, leaving any bacon grease in the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season salmon with salt and pepper, then place in the pan over medium heat skin-side up. Allow to cook, flipping and finishing skin-side down until cooked through. About 3-4 minutes per side depending on thickness. Set salmon on a plate and tent foil over the top to keep warm.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the same pan, add onion and garlic over medium-high heat. Allow to cook until garlic is fragrant, about 1 minute.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the chicken stock, tomato paste and heavy cream, stirring together. Allow to come to a boil to thicken up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once sauce has thickened, add in the basil, lemon zest, and bacon. Stir to combine. Season with salt and pepper as needed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate pan, add olive oil over medium-high heat. Once hot, add in the zucchini noodles and season with salt and pepper. Cook for 1-2 minutes or until just starting to soften.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the zoodles into the sauce and stir to coat zoodles.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Salmon-Zoodles-in-Creamy-Bacon-Tomato-Sauce-8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve the zoodles immediately with the salmon over the top. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/salmon-zoodles-in-creamy-bacon-tomato-sauce/#wprm-recipe-56724-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
